        <briefdescription>
<para>Constructor. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aMinimumDuration</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The minimum duration for a maneuver. Defaults to std::nullopt. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aMaximumManeuverDurationAndStrategy</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The maximum duration for a maneuver, along with the strategy to use when it is violated. Defaults to std::nullopt. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aMinimumSeparation</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The minimum separation between maneuvers. Defaults to std::nullopt. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aMaximumDutyCycle</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The maximum duty cycle as numerator and denominator. For example, {Duration::Minutes(40.0), Duration::Minutes(98.0)} represents a maximum maneuvering time of 40 minutes over any 98 minutes interval. Defaults to std::nullopt. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aConstantLocalOrbitalFrameEnforcement</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If provided, maneuvers will be forced to be constant in the given local orbital frame, meaning: every time a maneuver is computed by the guidance law, its mean direction in said local orbital frame is computed and the maneuver is made constant in that direction. The optional angle sets the maximum allowed angular offset between the original maneuver and its mean direction; if it is ever surpassed, an error is raised. If std::nullopt, no such check is performed (i.e. any maneuver is allowed to be made constant, regardless of how variable it might be in the local orbital frame). Defaults to std::nullopt. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
